  "13": {
   "hash": "dc1dc3c5cf12b8e9",
   "takes": [
    "5dc7eac1c5fcd0984145",
    "845eec29e2264d0d05fe",
    "4037aaa1cbebcf1ba4e2",
    "1c4b954ea64f7b785530",
    "6d3adc045764280dea24",
    "56a89efae67eff114150"
   ],
   "duration": 27.606,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Now comes the part that makes ownership a design tool.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 3.508
    },
    {
     "text": "A signature tells you what a call does to your value... without opening the body.",
     "start": 3.928,
     "end": 9.019
    },
    {
     "text": "Take the type itself, and the function owns it.",
     "start": 9.739,
     "end": 12.891
    },
    {
     "text": "Take a shared reference, and the function borrows it. Any number of borrows at once.",
     "start": 13.311,
     "end": 18.128
    },
    {
     "text": "Take a mutable reference, and the borrow is exclusive. Nobody else may touch the value meanwhile.",
     "start": 18.549,
     "end": 23.634
    },
    {
     "text": "Return the type, and ownership comes back to the caller.",
     "start": 24.054,
     "end": 27.256
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.2,
   "true_peak": -1.8,
   "wpm": 163,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "14": {
   "hash": "e82346d03aa11f9e",
   "takes": [
    "ede3ea26a41bed09208a",
    "a3d15b146a3dfedbc2d9",
    "1f7476b1e27c497874ae",
    "82fb14e101453bd404f5",
    "ac44080717e2c4e02f50",
    "94d6a1071c73f3075d30"
   ],
   "duration": 32.419,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Methods sign the same contract, in the receiver.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 4.261
    },
    {
     "text": "The length method takes a shared reference. It reads.",
     "start": 4.681,
     "end": 8.738
    },
    {
     "text": "The push-string method takes a mutable reference. It mutates.",
     "start": 9.158,
     "end": 12.647
    },
    {
     "text": "The method that turns a string into bytes takes the string itself. It consumes it.",
     "start": 13.067,
     "end": 18.022
    },
    {
     "text": "And consuming isn't copying. It returns a vector on the very same buffer. Zero allocations.",
     "start": 18.742,
     "end": 24.876
    },
    {
     "text": "Even the plus operator is a contract. It consumes the left side, and appends into its buffer, growing it if needed.",
     "start": 25.296,
     "end": 32.069
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.8,
   "wpm": 144,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
