    "937771bef24a6ba2fc9b",
    "8ca73bcee974faae089b"
   ],
   "duration": 33.65,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Now let's read the compiler's error properly.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 2.834
    },
    {
     "text": "It has three spans, and they go in a fixed order.",
     "start": 3.254,
     "end": 6.764
    },
    {
     "text": "One. Why it moved. Vector of bytes isn't Copy.",
     "start": 7.184,
     "end": 12.409
    },
    {
     "text": "Two. Where it moved. The call.",
     "start": 12.829,
     "end": 15.915
    },
    {
     "text": "Three. The later use that broke the rule.",
     "start": 16.335,
     "end": 19.393
    },
    {
     "text": "Each span is a place to fix it. Plain data? Derive Copy. Or borrow at the move site. Or use the value first.",
     "start": 20.113,
     "end": 28.116
    },
    {
     "text": "The note even says the signature may be wrong. And the clone suggestion? Last resort.",
     "start": 28.536,
     "end": 33.3
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.6,
   "true_peak": -1.8,
   "wpm": 141,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "17": {
   "hash": "cfa150f3dc0ca35d",
   "takes": [
    "43be67b1eb6bc6f47748",
    "fdceb3eb6c8785cdd60b",
    "a7e2d6ec4f3f23fce8d5",
    "27e7978157d46859915d",
    "9e2e7ffff7513160bc9f"
   ],
   "duration": 29.381,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "A second error. The move-while-borrowed error.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 3.3
    },
    {
     "text": "You borrowed a header out of the batch... and then moved the batch, while that borrow was still alive.",
     "start": 3.72,
     "end": 9.824
    },
    {
     "text": "A borrow lasts until its last use. Not to the end of the block.",
     "start": 10.244,
     "end": 16.539
    },
    {
     "text": "So finish with the header first, and the move fits.",
     "start": 17.259,
     "end": 20.863
    },
    {
     "text": "The compiler suggests cloning here too... a million bytes copied to keep four. Copying just the four bytes is the better copy.",
     "start": 21.283,
     "end": 29.031
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.6,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 149,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "18": {
   "hash": "e49c61c871af718a",
   "takes": [
    "75dbbc3f3cf241e1d7e9",
    "9d347706e7b429b4efbf",
    "f2dd3eb5f104a4f19be8"
   ],
   "duration": 10.757,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "A loop is a path... that comes back.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 3.768
    },
    {
     "text": "Ship takes the batch by value, and the loop runs three times.",
     "start": 4.188,
     "end": 8.714
    },
    {
     "text": "What happens?",
     "start": 9.534,
     "end": 10.407
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 123,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "18a": {
   "hash": "a5d5d0dd876494a3",
   "takes": [
    "553857d697f34483f409",
    "c18dd4aaae02ccae94e6"
   ],
   "duration": 13.164,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "It doesn't compile. On the second pass through the loop, the batch is already gone.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 5.598
    },
    {
     "text": "The same rule means a for loop over a vector consumes it. Iterate over a reference to borrow.",
     "start": 6.818,
     "end": 12.814
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.3,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 150,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "19": {
   "hash": "a46a4be02ed8dc8f",
   "takes": [
    "06a1e1b604c201c6fd25",
    "44f820e843015544ba6a",
    "dc9e51b076288c58eb19",
    "a8e0a074645b81d3c33d",
    "00863d617140af332a2e",
    "7ee53690dee9b91c0f3a"
   ],
   "duration": 28.908,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Back to the batch.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 1.206
    },
    {
     "text": "Read the original error by its spans. The vector moved at the call, and was used after.",
     "start": 1.626,
     "end": 7.164
    },
    {
     "text": "If ship only reads, the signature was wrong. Take a slice, pass a reference. Zero allocations. Zero bytes copied.",
     "start": 7.584,
     "end": 15.389
    },
    {
     "text": "If ship must own the batch, read the length first and move last. Also zero.",
     "start": 15.809,
     "end": 20.966
    },
    {
     "text": "The clone was correct code... paying a million bytes per batch for nothing.",
     "start": 21.686,
     "end": 25.875
    },
    {
     "text": "The right signature costs nothing.",
     "start": 26.295,
     "end": 28.558
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.6,
   "true_peak": -1.8,
   "wpm": 152,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
